# Regex patterns, one per line, matched against repository-relative paths.
# .kore/ holds local key material; no scanner may ever read it.
^\.kore/
(^|/)node_modules/
(^|/)dist/
(^|/)bin/
(^|/)coverage/
# SOPS-encrypted files are expected ciphertext (ENC[...] values), not leaked secrets.
\.enc\.yaml$
# Vendored upstream Keycloak CRD: the JDBC detector reports a documentation example sentence in an upstream description (no host, no credential). The current file is trimmed and scans clean; the line stays only while the branch history holds the original, and can go once the change is squashed.
(^|/)infra/charts/keycloak-operator/templates/crd-keycloaks\.yaml$
# The signed-in BFF's session database URL (issue 1841). The JDBC detector reports credential-free jdbc:postgresql:// strings: the chart's URL is built from $(SESSION_DB_*) references to the claim's connection Secret, and two specs name an example host. None holds a password (that is read by Secret reference). The history holds the first commit, so the paths stay excluded until the change is squashed.
(^|/)infra/charts/golden-path-workload/templates/workload\.yaml$
(^|/)templates/kotlin-bff/src/test/kotlin/dev/kore/bff/session/SessionStoreSettingsTest\.kt$
(^|/)tools/kore/integration/config/golden-path-signin-session-chart\.spec\.ts$
